# feat: vgpu public API rewrite

**Branch:** `feat/vgpu-rewrite` → `main` · **Merge base:** `00c2c7f` · **Tip:** `c51a8e8`
**Scope:** 108 commits · 734 files · +28,891 / −12,487 lines

---

## Summary

This PR replaces the entire `@vgpu/render` surface — `App.create`, `RapidRenderer`, `material()`, and the old `RenderPass` — with a coherent public API exported from the `vgpu` package. The previous thick renderer mixed global device state, implicit material declarations, and surface management into a single opaque layer that made it hard to reason about bind-group lifetimes, pipeline caching, or GPU resource ownership. The rewrite removes all of that.

The new design is organized around a single **core rule**: every resource has an explicit owner, an explicit identity, and an explicit target. The `Gpu` interface is the only entry point. It produces typed, composable objects — `Pass`, `Draw`, `Compute`, `Bundle`, `Target` — that can be handed to a frame loop at any level of abstraction without leaking implementation details upward.

vgpu is layered: **`vgpu/core`** (thin WebGPU wrappers) → **`vgpu`** (main API with WGSL reflection) → **`vgpu/scene`** (geometry/camera helpers). Lower layers are always accessible and interoperable. The rewrite also introduces **ShaderSource** as a first-class contract for pure WGSL modules, a **nine-pattern performance playbook** baked into the docs and LLM skill, public **instancing** via `DrawOptions.instances`, a documentation standard enforced by a snippet compiler, and a full rewrite of `apps/docs`. Simultaneously, `@vgpu/render` is trimmed to four slim tooling subpaths (`./edit`, `./inspect`, `./utils`, `./perf`) — its old surface primitives are gone.

---

## 1. Public surface hygiene

All three entrypoints (`vgpu`, `vgpu/node`, `vgpu/mock`) export `Draw`, `Pass`, `Frame`, `FramePass`, and `FrameRunner` as **types only**. No implementation class is part of the public surface.

```ts
// packages/vgpu-api/src/index.ts (browser entrypoint)
export type { Draw, DrawOptions, DrawCallOptions, DrawLayoutOptions, MeshLike } from "./draw.ts";
export type { Frame, FramePass, FramePassOptions, FrameLoopHandle, FrameLoopOptions, FrameRunner } from "./frame.ts";
export type { Pass, PassOptions } from "./pass.ts";
// every one of these is `export type` — no implementation value is exported
```

Internals are hidden via `WeakMap`. `Pass` stores its backing `InternalDraw` in a module-private map (see `packages/vgpu-api/src/pass.ts`):

```ts
// packages/vgpu-api/src/pass.ts
const passImpls = new WeakMap<Pass, InternalDraw>();

export interface Pass {
  readonly gpu: GPURenderPipeline | undefined;
  set(values: SetBag): this;
  draw(opts?: DrawCallOptions & { readonly target?: Target }): void;
}
```

Callers receive a `Pass` interface value. `passImpls`, `InternalDraw`, `InternalPass`, `encodeDraw`, `passDraw` are never exported. The same pattern applies to `Draw` (backed by a `DrawState` record) and `Frame`/`FramePass` (construction is internal to `FrameRunner`). `BundleBackReference`, `BundleBackReferenceRegistry`, and `BundleStaleEvent` are internal bundle bookkeeping — not exported.

---

## 2. The new API

The `Gpu` interface (see `packages/vgpu-api/src/gpu.ts`) is shared across browser, Node, and mock entrypoints. It is created via `init()`.

### Fullscreen passes — `gpu.pass` (main API, `vgpu`)

For fragment-only effects: `gpu.pass()` injects a built-in fullscreen vertex shader so the caller only writes a fragment entry point. Whether the supplied shader already contains a `@vertex` entry is detected via WGSL reflection (`reflectSource(...).entryPoints`), not string scanning. Group 0 bindings are auto-reflected; values are set by name via `set()`.

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/pass.ts, packages/vgpu-api/src/gpu.ts
import { init } from "vgpu";
import WAVE_WGSL from "./wave.wgsl"; // ShaderSource { version: 1, wgsl: "..." }

const gpu = await init(canvas);

const wave = gpu.pass(WAVE_WGSL, { set: { time: 0, speed: 2 } });

gpu.frame.loop((f) => {
  wave.set({ time: gpu.time });
  f.pass({ target: gpu.screen }, (p) => p.draw(wave));
});
```

`gpu.pass()` accepts `string | ShaderSource` — a raw WGSL string or an imported `.wgsl` file.

### Explicit draw calls — `gpu.draw` (main API, `vgpu`)

For mesh rendering with explicit control over instances, targets, and dynamic offsets. Group 0 is auto-reflected; higher groups are claimed via `draw.group()`.

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/draw.ts, packages/vgpu-api/src/gpu.ts
import { init } from "vgpu";
import { box } from "vgpu/scene";

const gpu = await init(canvas);
const scene = gpu.target({ format: "rgba16float", depth: true, msaa: true });

const cube = gpu.draw({
  shader: LIT_WGSL,              // string | ShaderSource
  mesh: gpu.mesh(box()),
  instances: 1000,               // DrawOptions.instances: default instance count
  targets: [scene],              // pre-warms pipeline at construction time
  set: { albedo: myTex },
});

gpu.frame.loop((f) => {
  cube.set({ model: transforms });
  f.pass({ target: scene, clear: [0, 0, 0, 1] }, (p) => p.draw(cube));
});
```

`DrawOptions` fields relevant to instancing (see `packages/vgpu-api/src/draw.ts`):

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `shader` | `string \| ShaderSource` | WGSL source or imported module |
| `mesh` | `MeshLike` | Vertex/index buffer descriptor |
| `instances` | `number` | Default instance count per draw call |
| `vertices` | `number` | Default vertex count (non-indexed, no mesh) |
| `firstInstance` | `number` | Default `firstInstance` offset |
| `targets` | `Target[]` | Pre-warms pipeline for each target at construction |
| `set` | `SetBag` | Initial binding values by WGSL name |

Per-call overrides live in `DrawCallOptions`: `instances`, `vertices`, `firstVertex`, `firstInstance`, `offsets`.

### Compute — `gpu.compute` (main API, `vgpu`)

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/compute.ts
const sim = gpu.compute(SIM_WGSL, { set: { dt: 0.016 } });

gpu.frame.loop(() => {
  sim.set({ dt: gpu.deltaTime });
  sim.dispatch(64);           // dispatchWorkgroups(64, 1, 1)
});
```

`Compute.dispatch(x, y?, z?)` builds the command encoder, sets bind groups from the reflected layout, and submits immediately. Storage aliasing is checked before every dispatch — a writable buffer bound twice throws `VGPU-STORAGE-ALIASING` with a fix-it.

### Bundles — `gpu.bundle` (main API, `vgpu`)

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/bundle.ts
const staticScene = gpu.bundle({ target: scene }, (b) => {
  b.draw(floor);
  b.draw(walls);
});

gpu.frame.loop((f) =>
  f.pass({ target: scene }, (p) => {
    p.bundles(staticScene); // GPURenderBundle replay
    p.draw(player);
  })
);
```

Bundles snapshot the target's color formats, depth format, and MSAA count at record time. Replaying after a resize or after a `Draw`'s bind group changes throws `VGPU-R3-BUNDLE-STALE` with the exact binding name and a re-recording fix-it.

### Scene helpers — `vgpu/scene`

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/scene.ts
import { box, icosphere, perspectiveCamera, orbit } from "vgpu/scene";

const mesh = gpu.mesh(icosphere({ subdivisions: 4 }));
const cam = perspectiveCamera({ fov: 60, aspect: 16 / 9, near: 0.1, far: 1000 });
const controller = orbit(cam, canvas);
```

`vgpu/scene` exports geometry factories (`box`, `sphere`, `capsule`, `cylinder`, `torus`, `plane`, `icosphere`, `cone`, `disk`, `ring`, `dodecahedron`, `icosahedron`, `octahedron`, `tetrahedron`, `fullscreenQuad`), camera helpers (`perspectiveCamera`, `orthographicCamera`), `orbit`, and math utilities (`degToRad`, `srgb`, `Mat4`, `Vec3`).

### Node / mock entrypoints

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/node.ts — Dawn via @vgpu/adapter-node
import { init } from "vgpu/node";
const gpu = await init();        // headless, no canvas
```

```ts
// See packages/vgpu-api/src/mock.ts — in-memory stub
import { init, getMockGPUDeviceInstrumentation } from "vgpu/mock";
const gpu = await init();
const

