## Summary

Adds a dedicated analytics and developer-health workspace for every Hosted Game, built on Hosted Game Standard v1 lifecycle events, server-authoritative runs, Distribution reward records, PPPM lifecycle records, release snapshots, and privacy-limited browser telemetry.

This PR is intentionally stacked on PR #1105 (`feature/hosted-game-standard-sdk-v1-20260715`) so its diff contains only analytics and diagnostics work. After #1105 merges into `integration-from-repair-20260628`, this PR should be retargeted to the integration branch and revalidated.

## Game analytics workspace

Merchant route:

- `/merchant-game-analytics.php?game={hosted-game-public-id}`

Admin route:

- `/admin/hosted-game-analytics.php?game={hosted-game-public-id}`

Each Hosted Games inventory card/row receives an Analytics action.

Metrics include:

- game loads;
- unique and connected players;
- runs started and completed;
- qualification and abandonment rates;
- average play duration;
- average, highest, and lowest scores;
- repeat-player rate;
- rewards queued, delivered, failed, claimed, and redeemed;
- inventory consumed;
- allocated reward value and value per qualified player;
- daily load/run/completion/error trends;
- device, browser, and viewport breakdowns;
- Standard event and level funnels;
- release-version comparisons.

## Persistent release attribution

Adds `hosted_game_run_observability` to snapshot:

- release public ID and version;
- SDK and game versions;
- privacy-limited client context;
- qualification and abandonment timestamps;
- measured play duration.

Historical runs therefore remain attributed to the release that produced them after later releases are activated.

## Error monitoring and health reporting

Adds grouped diagnostics and occurrence history for:

- JavaScript runtime errors;
- unhandled promise rejections;
- SDK request failures and slow actions;
- asset-loading failures;
- manifest warnings;
- slow startup;
- webhook failures;
- database failures;
- reward-delivery failures.

Diagnostics are grouped by SHA-256 fingerprint across game, release, browser, category, normalized message, and first stack line. Groups support Open, Resolved, Ignored, and Reopen actions.

## Telemetry security

- Telemetry passes from the opaque-origin game iframe through the trusted parent shell.
- CSRF, active-game lookup, event allowlisting, JSON limits, and session rate limits remain enforced.
- Run-linked telemetry requires the signed-in player, game/run ownership, and the one-time run token.
- No raw IP address, email address, API key, webhook secret, database credential, cookie, or CSRF token is stored in analytics records.

## Diagnostics export

Authorized Merchant and Admin users can export a ZIP containing:

- `summary.json`;
- `diagnostic-groups.csv`;
- `diagnostic-occurrences.csv`;
- `README.txt`.

Exports are capped at 5,000 groups and 10,000 occurrences and omit secrets and direct contact data.

## Permissions

Merchant:

- `merchant.hosted_games.analytics.view`
- `merchant.hosted_games.diagnostics.manage`

Admin:

- `admin.hosted_games.analytics.view`
- `admin.hosted_games.diagnostics.manage`

Merchant APIs enforce game ownership. Admin APIs require the dedicated permission or settings-management authority.

